{"name":"Balance","hex":"#d1dbc2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Balance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The constellation and zodiacal sign Libra."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Balance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Balance (ability)","blocks":[{"text":"Balance in biomechanics, is an ability to maintain the line of gravity of a body within the base of support with minimal postural sway. Sway is the horizontal movement of the centre of gravity even when a person is standing still. A certain amount of sway is essential and inevitable due to small perturbations within the body or from external triggers. An increase in sway is not necessarily an indicator of dysfunctional balance so much as it is an indicator of decreased sensorimotor control."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Model_Balancing.jpg/330px-Model_Balancing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balance_(ability)","wikidata":"Q1530280"},{"title":"Balance (accounting)","blocks":[{"text":"In banking and accounting, the balance is the amount of money owed on an account."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balance_(accounting)","wikidata":"Q1365641"},{"title":"Balance (Van Halen album)","blocks":[{"text":"Balance is the tenth studio album by American rock band Van Halen, released on January 24, 1995, by Warner Bros. Records. The album is the last of the band's four studio releases to feature Sammy Hagar as the lead singer. It is also the final Van Halen album to feature bassist Michael Anthony in its entirety. Balance reached number 1 on the U.S. Billboard 200 in February 1995 and reached triple platinum status on May 12, 2004, by selling more than three million copies in the US. \"The Seventh Seal\" was nominated for a Grammy for Best Hard Rock Performance."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e7/Van_Halen_-_Balance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balance_(Van_Halen_album)","wikidata":"Q1753419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Wine_glass_tower.jpg/500px-Wine_glass_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Wine_glass_tower.jpg/1280px-Wine_glass_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Wine_glass_tower.jpg/500px-Wine_glass_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A waiter balancing wine glasses","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWine_glass_tower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg/500px-Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg/1280px-Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg/500px-Plank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Balance Training","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlank_on_a_pair_of_medicine_balls.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Gyut%C3%B6_Ramoche_University_main_gompa.jpg/500px-Gyut%C3%B6_Ramoche_University_main_gompa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Gyut%C3%B6_Ramoche_University_main_gompa.jpg/1280px-Gyut%C3%B6_Ramoche_University_main_gompa.jpg?utm_sourc